= Semantic network — Simple =

A '''semantic network''' represents ideas or things as a network of connections.

For example:

<pre>
Canary → is a → Bird
Bird → has → Wings
</pre>

The nodes are concepts or entities.

The links explain how they are related.

Semantic networks were used in early artificial intelligence and in theories of human memory.

They are related to modern [[Knowledge graph/Simple|knowledge graphs]], but they are not the same thing as the [[Semantic Web/Simple|Semantic Web]].

The meaning of each link still needs to be defined. Drawing an arrow between two ideas does not automatically tell a computer what it may logically infer.

